<body>
    <h1>Employee access general pain points</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h3 id=3D"Employeeaccessgeneralpainpoints-PainPoints">Pain Points</=
h3>
<p>1. Process inefficiency:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"2f6ce76b-4b6c-4bdb-bd8c-1aa9ee403947">ID Custodians and I=
D Admins will have to repeat the process to approve requests, set up user a=
ccounts and reply to requestors as many times as how many applications are =
applicable to the employee</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"bd7bbcd5-144f-4195-87ae-30631cfed6e6">New Compass (CX, NC=
E) user access requests are not available on Service Now, increasing the ch=
ance of being missed and efforts to track down the progress</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"baeb4962-be8c-4e31-ae6c-7baa2bf3a5b4">As a result, it adv=
ersely impacts the productivity, extends the employee onboarding/offboardin=
g and access request cycle, and lower employee satisfaction.</li>
</ul>
<p>2. Access matrix inconsistency:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"6beac4a8-62f3-49e1-9ee8-859c0773317a">Maintenance challen=
ge - There is not a clear cadency of access matrix maintenance or governanc=
e.&nbsp;&nbsp;=20
  <ul>
   <li>For instance, when internal groups are updated (e.g. new groups adde=
d, several groups combined), all access matrices are supposed to be updated=
 to align to the new internal group list. As there is no strict governance,=
 the access matrices may not be updated within a reasonable time frame or n=
ot updated at all, causing misalignment in access provisioning easily.</li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ab7cba67-0830-47b4-8e0f-c7090c93322b">Repository challeng=
e - There is no central location of access matrices&nbsp;=20
  <ul>
   <li>Access matrices are often shared by the ID custodians (owners) to th=
e ID admins (users) via email or other means, rather than sharing through a=
 central location, causing versioning issue easily&nbsp;</li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"a036ea67-6393-4949-9cb3-fb1716b8f999">Cross platform acce=
ss provisioning challenge - There is no way to cross-reference access provi=
sions for integrated systems&nbsp;=20
  <ul>
   <li><span>For instance, as SOMA is integrated to the New Compass platfor=
m as a core service, the access provision of SOMA on Compass must conform t=
o that on SZ to ensure an cohesive access. However, as the access matrices =
are driven separately, </span>there is no 360 degree overview across integr=
ated platforms to ensure consistency.</li>
   <li>As a result, if the access provisions are misaligned, there will be =
a user experience interruption.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>
  </ul></li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<p>For New Compass employee access only =E2=80=93&nbsp;<br>
  3. Security risk:</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"3b53f944-47d6-4f45-a11b-8c4737cb7fed">The Access matrix g=
overning NCE employee access is not yet conformed to the access matrix temp=
late published by Enterprise IAM</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"638973a9-9323-4f7a-8f7f-6e5e953c7f3c">As the NCE offboard=
ing request is not integrated to the Service Now workflow (via IIQ), it is =
sometimes missed, creating an opportunity of access breaching by departed e=
mployees</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ee1f89a0-7a5f-482d-a030-3d3e1d8657ba">New Compass is espe=
cially vulnerable because, unlikely other applications at the Bank, it auth=
enticates employee user accounts via the Okta external (NBIN) tenant rather=
 than the Azure token obtained through the Bank's network</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"8dc8d0b4-1d9f-43ae-abe3-111ea9c21171">NCE is not equipped=
 with employee access attestation while the existing R2 manual operation an=
d IIQ automated process are not applicable to NCE</li>
</ul>
<p>4. User password challenge:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"66a668ea-2e26-4448-b1a7-ae1f2a3a9964">Unlike accessing ot=
her apps on the Bank's network, employee accessing NCE cannot single sign i=
n but will be required to provide their user credential and an one-time cod=
e to log in, introducing login churns and challenges due to forgotten passw=
ords</li>
</ul>
<p>5. Missing capabilities:</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b7ee1e82-1515-41ae-9bed-7e35bb806cad">Ways for NBIN Suppo=
rt team to use a user credential to log in as external clients, via Interne=
t - to be addressed in requirement-6</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"c39daea2-1de0-418e-95eb-063e9b5151a4">For firm security s=
tewards, being able to get the audit trail of access changes, login history=
 for their users - to be addressed in self-serve user admin feature</li>
</ul>
<p>6. Violation:</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"8c61a3e7-4a05-4765-93b9-39ac37649049">Someone still uses =
NPAD to manage legacy Compass user accounts. Problems: no field validation,=
 causing security breach easily; not connected to integrated systems as it =
is supposed to be.</li>
</ul>
<p>7. MyIT/Service Now submission issues:</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"3e100cb2-f75b-4b7e-8768-f20ac21eaa34">Users sometimes sub=
mit request for 1019-R1 access as 5213-R2 access accidentally</li>
</ul>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
